It was recently brought to my attention (in #dnethack) that 
there is a bug relating to long engravings in a square. I 
have verified the bug's existence in dNAOhack, but from 
discussions in #dnethack and what I can see in the sources 
it seems that the bug also exists in NAO nethack.

The source of the bug seems to be that engravings cannot 
exceed 256 characters (the length of the string buffer), 
but players are not given any feedback that hints at this
limit. In particular, players can elect to add to an 
engraving that is already 256 characters long, and the 
engraving process appears to work as normal (wand charges
are expended, tools are dulled, multi-turn engravings 
immobilize the character for the expected time, messages
indicating success or failure are printed). However, at 
the last moment the total length of the finished 
engraving is chopped down to the size of the input 
buffer, with no message:

if (oep) Strcpy(buf, oep->engr_txt);

(void) strncat(buf, ebuf, (BUFSZ - (int)strlen(buf) - 1));

make_engr_at(u.ux, u.uy, buf, (moves - multi), type);

(Where oep is the original engraving in your space, buf is
a character buffer, ebuf is a character buffer containing 
the text to be added, and BUFSZ is 256.)
________________________________________________________

People seem to generally notice this bug while attempting 
to use multiple dust engraved Elbereths to fight with. 
The bug makes it seem as though Elbereth fails to work 
once the length of the engraving goes above a certain 
limit (when in fact the later 'Elbereth's are simply 
not added in the first place).
________________________________________________________
I have two questions:

1) This IS a bug which is generally known, right? I wasn't
able to find any reference to it online.

2) Obviously the existing behavior is wrong, since it 
consumes resources but does nothing. What should the proper
behavior be? The existing engraving code can easily handle 
engravings with up to ~2 billion characters, but should 2 
billion character engravings really be allowed in a single 
square?

